    "subject_name": "Mathematics",
    "chapter_id": "61602565bccda81624f5a071",
    "chapter_name": "Area Under Curves",
    "year": "2022",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let a curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;pass through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and the area of the region under this curve, above the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis and between the abscissae&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. If this curve also passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in the first quadrant, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given, the area of the region under this curve, above the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis and between the abscissae&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>y</mi><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>y</mi><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>Now differentiating both side w.r.t&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mtext>as&#160;given&#160;</mtext><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>y</mi><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></math></p><p>Now put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#8747;</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>So, solution is given by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>F</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math>Now given curve passes through &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So the equation of curve is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Now curve also passes through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1080</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}